  "provenance": "Real Home UI, not drawn mocks: unlocked git-archive copy of smart-upkeep main 3a02155f (live Home from the #90/#93/#89/#94 stack; later main 1800ae2 only hides the You're In Your Home card and does not change Home). Checksum-matched to that commit, unlocked with the official pagelock tool on the copy only, served on 127.0.0.1 with every external request aborted (Google Fonts CSS answered locally with the same Khand and Hind files; no analytics, no Supabase). Options are CSS or DOM overrides on the local unlocked copy only: one-viewport section height, larger existing content, longer existing lists, boxless Share, no See What's Included on plan tiles, and the new short lead Home Care, On Schedule. Plan lines are from the Legal-approved Home key points and existing What We Take Care Of / feature labels; And More is kept. No Street View. Headless Chromium at 390×844 (deck images, dsf 2, JPEG q90) and 360×640 plus 1280×800 (fit and crop QA). Section height vs viewport is recorded for every option at all three sizes. Nothing was submitted, paid, finished or sent.",
